[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 986,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 951,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148613,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 951,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) of the stomach is a gastric carcinoma showing squamous cell differentiation, characterized by keratinocyte-type cells with intercellular bridges and/or keratinization.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 987,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 952,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148614,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 952,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>80700/3 Squamous cell carcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 988,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 953,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148615,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 953,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B72.Y &amp; XH0945 Squamous cell carcinoma, NOS, of stomach</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 989,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 954,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148616,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 954,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 990,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 955,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148617,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 955,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Verrucous squamous cell carcinoma (80510/3)</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 991,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 956,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148618,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 956,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The upper, lower, and middle portions of the stomach are affected in decreasing order of frequency {24765539;27559983}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 992,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 957,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148619,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 957,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical features are the same as those of other gastric cancers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 993,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 958,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148620,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 958,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Limited data are available. Primary gastric SCC is rare, accounting for 0.04&ndash;0.5% of all gastric cancers {37719040;30788163}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 994,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 959,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148621,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 959,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 995,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 960,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148622,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 960,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Various mechanisms have been proposed, including malignant progression of squamous metaplasia, development from pluripotent stem cells or mucosal ectopic squamous nests, and squamous transdifferentiation of adenocarcinoma {24765539;25925374;37719040}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1002,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 967,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148623,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 967,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic appearance is the same as that of other gastric cancers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 996,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 961,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148624,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 961,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histology is similar to that of SCC of the oesophagus (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/72/13\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Oesophageal squamous cell carcinoma</em>) and other organs. The tumour shows uniform squamous cell differentiation without adenocarcinoma or other histology on thorough sampling. Exhaustive sampling to exclude another component is crucial, as is the exclusion of metastasis from SCC from another organ. Distal extension of an oesophageal SCC should be ruled out.</p>\r\n<p>Verrucous SCC has been recognized as a morphological subtype; the tumour is characterized by very well differentiated keratinizing squamous cells with minimal atypia, demonstrating coarse surface papillary projections and bulbous downgrowth {30761414}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 997,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 962,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148625,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 962,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal lavage cytology is used for staging gastric cancer and monitoring chemotherapy (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/72/27\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Gastric adenocarcinoma</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 998,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 963,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148626,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 963,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Limited data are available (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/72/27\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Gastric adenocarcinoma</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1001,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 966,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148627,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 966,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> histological evidence of squamous cell differentiation; proof of invasion.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> exclusion of metastasis from another organ.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 999,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 964,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148628,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 964,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gastric SCC frequently manifests at an advanced stage, associated with poor outcome. Spread to the liver is frequent in advanced disease {29390350;27559983;37719040}. For TNM staging, see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/72/27\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Gastric adenocarcinoma</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1000,
    "bookid": 72,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 965,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 148629,
        "bookId": 72,
        "chapterId": 28,
        "headingId": 965,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Because of the rarity of this entity, no specific prognostic features have been identified. Disease stage at diagnosis is probably the main determinant of prognosis {29390350;27559983;37719040}. Gastric SCC seems to behave more aggressively than adenocarcinoma of the same disease stage {29390350;30788163}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-06-09T11:26:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]